  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Clink",
    "overview": "Everything in Clinkr is built around one physical moment: you tap, it clinks, the ring fills. Shapes are round and chunky, fills are solid, and every add answers with a haptic. A tap on a drink button also clinks, with a short spring. The system exists for a thumb in the dark, so one large target and one glance beat any detail that needs a steady hand.\n\nThe Watch is the built expression of this world: saturated color on pure black, where the off pixels disappear and only the content remains. Density is low and scale is loud. A single number and a ring fill Tonight, and the drink colors carry the meaning so the screen needs few words. Color does the playing, and the shapes stay simple enough that it never turns noisy.\n\nOn the iPhone the History screen and the Night Recap are built. Its light theme, with warm cream and a sticker look, is still provisional elsewhere, and is marked as such throughout this file. Shipped values live in `Shared/`, and the wider design system lives at https://claude.ai/artifact/MUR9q8zqsWysfgui8mdNsh. Keep all three in step.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Solid, saturated fills on black, with no outlines or gradients on the Watch",
      "Round everywhere: pills, large-radius cards, round-capped ring segments",
      "SF Pro Rounded at heavy weights, with nothing on the Watch lighter than semibold",
      "Flat on the Watch, with depth from tone alone",
      "Motion under 400ms and reduced under Reduce Motion, with a haptic on every add"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Fizz Rule",
        "body": "One `fizz` element per screen. Its rarity is what makes it the primary action.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fill, Not Text Rule",
        "body": "Pop colors are fills, never text. Anything on them uses `on-pop`, never white. A glyph may stand alone in its drink color on a dark `bg`, but never on cream.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Careful Alone Rule",
        "body": "`careful` always comes with an icon and words, and never shares a screen with a `fizz` fill, because the two sit close in hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Tint Rule",
        "body": "The system tint is `ink`, never a pop color, because the system draws it as text. In dark mode `ink` is cream, so no screen uses a system prominent button style (`.borderedProminent`, `.glassProminent`), which puts white on the tint. Primary actions use the design system's pills.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Friendly Nudge Rule",
        "body": "The water break nudge is drawn in `water`. A suggestion never borrows the look of an alert.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hero Shrinks First Rule",
        "body": "When space runs out, on a small Watch or at a large text size, the count shrinks before the caption and waters do. Labels stay readable.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Steady Count Rule",
        "body": "Counts always use tabular figures, so the number doesn't jump as it ticks up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Semibold Floor Rule",
        "body": "Nothing on the Watch is lighter than semibold.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Wrist Rule",
        "body": "No shadows on the Watch, ever. The `stickerShadow()` modifier draws nothing in dark mode, so it can't appear there. The one proposed exception is a glass Undo toast, if the prototype in #80 keeps it (see Liquid Glass).",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Content Stays Solid Rule",
        "body": "A drink color is never behind glass and never glass itself. Glass floats above content, never inside it. (Proposed.)",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glass Is Rare Rule",
